{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor appropriately escalated worsening colicky pain to emergency care, maintained urology as the priority, arranged timely specialist follow-up, tracked pending polyp pathology, and obtained a clear caregiver teach-back. However, RC3 had a minor privacy-chain omission because identifiable document photographs were requested without redaction instructions. RC5 also had a moderate execution error because the doctor supplied an unsupported 2–4 week medication duration despite incomplete prescribing and renal-function context; any minor/moderate chain error caps the grade at 2.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00266",
        "explanation": "The doctor closed with a concrete plan covering medication use, monitoring, repeat testing, emergency thresholds, and pathology follow-up.",
        "quote": "一两周后去复查，同时抽空把肠镜病理追回来。"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00280",
        "explanation": "The caregiver demonstrated receipt and ability to execute both the urology and pathology plans.",
        "quote": "我就先按门诊和您说的办"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The bounded episode ended after emergency evaluation and urology review, with repeat urine, renal-function and ultrasound testing assigned for 1–2 weeks, separate pathology follow-up, and explicit emergency contingencies. The plan was executable and received, although privacy handling and medication-duration advice were imperfect.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
